# The pipeline trace is an append-only ledger, so Prettier must not touch it.
#
# AGENTS.md requires one row per landed feature and forbids rewriting existing rows, because the
# ledger's value is that a past row reads today exactly as it read when it was written. Prettier
# formats Markdown tables by re-padding every column to the widest cell, so appending one wider row
# rewrites all the rows above it. That is a whitespace-only change and it still defeats the rule: it
# turns a one-line append into a whole-table diff, which is noise in review, a conflict magnet on any
# branch that also appends, and an audit trail that cannot be read as untouched.
#
# Excluding the file is what makes the append-only rule enforceable rather than aspirational. Rows are
# written by hand in the existing style and the columns do not need to line up, since Markdown renders
# a ragged table identically to a padded one.
docs/pipeline-trace.md
